   "title": "Link the Digikal knowledge base (DIG-340)",
   "body": "Documentation only, for [DIG-340](https://paperclip.digikal.com/DIG/issues/DIG-340): link this project to the canonical Digikal knowledge base, `https://repo.digikal.com/jawad/digikal-knowledge-base`. That repository was made canonical by DIG-339 (KB PR #1, merge `c5f3087`).\n\n**Changed:** CLAUDE.md. Each file gets an appended `## Digikal knowledge base` section. Existing instructions are unchanged, and managed blocks such as the `ai-engineering-governance` markers are left untouched.\n\n**What it says:**\n- links to the KB index, this project's page (`knowledge/projects/humm/README.md`), `CONTRIBUTING.md` and `knowledge/CONVENTIONS.md`\n- how to clone or find the KB, and what to read before work: architecture, status, decisions, design and the relevant domain hubs\n- how to judge `confidence`, `last_reviewed` and `sources`, and how to propose a sourced KB update after a decision or discovery\n- that this repository's own instructions and verified source keep their authority over KB pages\n- what to do without access to the private KB, with no credentials and no host-local paths\n\n**Base:** `main`, the repository's current default branch.\n\n**CI / release:** Forgejo Actions is disabled for this repository, so no workflow runs on the PR or the merge. No images, packages or deployments are affected.\n\n**Verification:** `git diff --check` is clean. Every KB link target returns HTTP 200 on KB `main` `c5f3087` through the authenticated raw route. Repo-specific checks are listed in the DIG-340 handoff.\n\n**Review:** DevGuru reviews adversarially (DIG-250). TechLead merges only after DevGuru approves.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
